\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces The last-30-min trade under one scorer: $\mathrm  {sign}(s)$ on the straddle, 15:30\nobreakspace  {}ET to the close, on the 866{} expiration days common to every row (3\nobreakspace  {}January\nobreakspace  {}2020 to 30\nobreakspace  {}April\nobreakspace  {}2024). Every forecast is turned into a variance by the 16:00-bar recalibration (Equation\nobreakspace  {}\eqref  {eq:close_opt_recal1600}). QLIKE: the recalibrated forecast's mean QLIKE at the $16{:}00$ bar; vs R: its percent difference from the reference R, the block-diagonal ridge (negative: more accurate), and the Diebold--Mariano statistic of that difference. Sharpe$_{\mathrm  {ann}}$: the portfolio's Sharpe ratio annualized by $\sqrt  {252}$ per trade day, at the 15:30 midpoint and at the crossed spread (bought at the ask, sold at the bid, at entry only; the position settles in cash). $\Delta $Sharpe: the midpoint Sharpe ratio minus that of R and of always short on the same days, with a 95\% paired interval (circular block bootstrap of the days, blocks of 21 days). Buys: the share of days the rule is long. Inputs: the input set of Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref {sec:close_option_methods} by its design name; panel\nobreakspace  {}A reads the paper's full design. Panel\nobreakspace  {}D holds one row per rung of the per-bar trees and LSTMs of Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref {sec:close_option_methods}, each LightGBM or the LSTM on \texttt  {live\_feasible}, so that consecutive rows differ in one thing; the other trees and input sets of every rung are counted in the text. $^{\dagger }$: the four columns still fitted on the earlier design panel (Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref {sec:close_option_methods}); H: the headline forecast (bold). The rows are selected from the closing-strategy master table, which scores 220{} forecasts the same way on the same days. }}{30}{table.caption.47}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:close_option_rules}{{7}{30}{The last-30-min trade under one scorer: $\mathrm {sign}(s)$ on the straddle, 15:30~ET to the close, on the \cmNdays {} expiration days common to every row (3~January~2020 to 30~April~2024). Every forecast is turned into a variance by the 16:00-bar recalibration (Equation~\eqref {eq:close_opt_recal1600}). QLIKE: the recalibrated forecast's mean QLIKE at the $16{:}00$ bar; vs R: its percent difference from the reference R, the block-diagonal ridge (negative: more accurate), and the Diebold--Mariano statistic of that difference. Sharpe$_{\mathrm {ann}}$: the portfolio's Sharpe ratio annualized by $\sqrt {252}$ per trade day, at the 15:30 midpoint and at the crossed spread (bought at the ask, sold at the bid, at entry only; the position settles in cash). $\Delta $Sharpe: the midpoint Sharpe ratio minus that of R and of always short on the same days, with a 95\% paired interval (circular block bootstrap of the days, blocks of 21 days). Buys: the share of days the rule is long. Inputs: the input set of Section~\ref {sec:close_option_methods} by its design name; panel~A reads the paper's full design. Panel~D holds one row per rung of the per-bar trees and LSTMs of Section~\ref {sec:close_option_methods}, each LightGBM or the LSTM on \texttt {live\_feasible}, so that consecutive rows differ in one thing; the other trees and input sets of every rung are counted in the text. $^{\dagger }$: the four columns still fitted on the earlier design panel (Section~\ref {sec:close_option_methods}); H: the headline forecast (bold). The rows are selected from the closing-strategy master table, which scores \cmMasterN {} forecasts the same way on the same days}{table.caption.47}{}}
