\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces One change at a time: paired differences between two forecasts of Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref {tab:close_option_rules} that differ in one thing (the step's ``to'' forecast minus its ``from'' forecast), on the same 866{} days under the 16:00-bar recalibration. QLIKE: percent difference in mean QLIKE at the $16{:}00$ bar with a 95\% day-block interval (negative: the ``to'' forecast is more accurate), and its Diebold--Mariano statistic. $\Delta $Sharpe: difference in the $\mathrm  {sign}(s)$ portfolio's annualized Sharpe ratio at the midpoint and at the crossed spread, with 95\% paired intervals on the resampled days of Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref {tab:close_option_rules}. Same side: the share of days the two forecasts take the same position. The first step changes the design, the training window and the penalty together; every other step changes one thing. Steps the master table also stores are reproduced by it exactly. The last five blocks are the rungs of the 16:00 re-run (Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref {sec:close_option_methods}) for LightGBM and the LSTM on \texttt  {live\_feasible}: the design row pairs the headline with its table before the re-run; the mask rows and the LSTM refit every ten sessions, whose unmasked or ten-session tables are not rows of Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref {tab:close_option_rules}, are read from the re-run's own paired comparisons (same days, same scorer and resampling); every other campaign step is recomputed here and reproduces the re-run's report. DM ---: not stored for that pair. }}{34}{table.caption.53}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:close_option_ladder}{{8}{34}{One change at a time: paired differences between two forecasts of Table~\ref {tab:close_option_rules} that differ in one thing (the step's ``to'' forecast minus its ``from'' forecast), on the same \cmNdays {} days under the 16:00-bar recalibration. QLIKE: percent difference in mean QLIKE at the $16{:}00$ bar with a 95\% day-block interval (negative: the ``to'' forecast is more accurate), and its Diebold--Mariano statistic. $\Delta $Sharpe: difference in the $\mathrm {sign}(s)$ portfolio's annualized Sharpe ratio at the midpoint and at the crossed spread, with 95\% paired intervals on the resampled days of Table~\ref {tab:close_option_rules}. Same side: the share of days the two forecasts take the same position. The first step changes the design, the training window and the penalty together; every other step changes one thing. Steps the master table also stores are reproduced by it exactly. The last five blocks are the rungs of the 16:00 re-run (Section~\ref {sec:close_option_methods}) for LightGBM and the LSTM on \texttt {live\_feasible}: the design row pairs the headline with its table before the re-run; the mask rows and the LSTM refit every ten sessions, whose unmasked or ten-session tables are not rows of Table~\ref {tab:close_option_rules}, are read from the re-run's own paired comparisons (same days, same scorer and resampling); every other campaign step is recomputed here and reproduces the re-run's report. DM ---: not stored for that pair}{table.caption.53}{}}
